WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:05.410
In the very first chapter of A Song of Ice
and Fire and the very first sequence of Game

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:11.140
of Thrones, we see mysterious icy figures
called “white walkers”, or “Others”.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:16.590
At first, we know nothing about them. Now,
five books and five seasons later, we… still

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:21.079
know almost nothing. But we “do know some
things”, so let’s look at what we’ve

00:00:21.079 --> 00:00:26.449
got and try to work out what the Others are,
what they want, and what’ll happen.

00:00:26.449 --> 00:00:30.669
The Others appear as “white shadows” “in
the darkness”, “Tall” and “gaunt”

00:00:30.669 --> 00:00:34.410
with “Bright … blue” eyes. They “come
when it’s cold”, in the night, or else

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:39.289
they bring the cold and darkness when they
come. Old Nan calls them “dead things”,

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:43.260
Sam calls them “monsters”, and Stannis
calls them “Demons made of snow and ice

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.469
and cold”, but when one’s killed we see
they’re “creatures” made of “blood”

00:00:47.469 --> 00:00:51.550
and “flesh” and “bone”. George Martin
has said that they’re “not dead” but

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:57.810
“a different sort of life” – “strange,
beautiful … inhuman, elegant, dangerous”.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:02.359
In the show, the walkers look more or less
like really old men with wrinkled skin, white

00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:07.060
beards, black nails, and bad teeth. Either
way, the Others clearly aren’t “dead things”

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:11.880
or “demons” but living creatures. They
speak, in a language of their own. They laugh,

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:16.060
they “screech” in pain , in the show
they show shock and anger. They make things

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:21.220
out of ice. So the Others are intelligent,
with emotion and maybe culture. They might

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:28.780
not be the monsters that they seem. That said,
they do a lot of killing.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.920
The Others wear “rippl[ing] … shift[ing]”
armour that can make them near-“invisible”,

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.259
and wield “strange pale sword[s]” so
sharp they can “slice … through ringmail

00:01:36.259 --> 00:01:41.219
as if it were silk”. They fight effortlessly, mercilessly, “lightning quick” and

00:01:41.219 --> 00:01:45.539
with the strength, in the show, to throw men
like ragdolls. “their … swords are so

00:01:45.539 --> 00:01:49.719
cold they shatter steel”, and their armour
protects them from most blades – they seem

00:01:49.719 --> 00:01:56.219
unstoppable. But they can be killed with obsidian,
also called dragonglass. Sam stabs an Other

00:01:56.219 --> 00:02:00.609
with an obsidian dagger, and the walker “melt[s]
away“, its fingers smoking where they touch

00:02:00.609 --> 00:02:05.320
obsidian. It’s also hinted that Valyrian
steel swords can kill walkers , and we see

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:10.530
this in the show – Jon Snow’s Valyrian
steel sword disintegrates an Other into icy

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:15.340
CGI. Others also apparently “don’t like
fire” – which probably means they’d

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:21.379
really hate dragons.
The Others resurrect the dead as “wights”,

00:02:21.379 --> 00:02:26.230
basically zombies controlled by the Others. Wights are “slow clumsy things”, “with

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:30.650
blue eyes and cold black hands”, though
in the show they’re sometimes skeletal and

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:35.709
fast . Wights don’t speak , and seem to
have no humanity left – though they seem

00:02:35.709 --> 00:02:41.590
to keep some memories. The Others make wights
out of “men … women … children” – and

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:45.810
animals – walkers “ride dead horses”, send a bear into battle , and animate a

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:51.459
raven. The Others use wights to fight for
them, and they’re very dangerous. Wights

00:02:51.459 --> 00:02:56.080
seem stronger than living men, able to “[lift
a man] in the air by the throat and near [rip]

00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:00.250
the head off him”. In the show they tear
through timber with their bare hands, they

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:04.909
fall off a cliff and keep on running. They
don’t seem to feel pain. Even losing their

00:03:04.909 --> 00:03:09.750
head won’t stop them , and if a hand is
cut off, the hand will keep moving. Unlike

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:13.980
the Others, wights aren’t hurt by obsidian. The only way to stop them is to chop them

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:19.040
into bits , or to burn them. Wights are really
flammable, “burst[ing] into flame” from

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.200
even a little touch of fire. So one wight
isn’t all that bad, but at the Fist of the

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:28.379
First Men, and at Hardhome in the show, they
come in a huge “swarm”, an unstoppable

00:03:28.379 --> 00:03:34.569
“tide of [the] living dead”, all controlled
by the icy white walkers.

00:03:34.569 --> 00:03:38.959
So what do the Others want? What are they
doing? Well, they’ve been killing a lot

00:03:38.959 --> 00:03:44.030
of humans. In Book 1 they kill some wildlings,
and some men of the Night’s Watch , and

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:48.409
they send wights after the Lord Commander
and acting First Ranger at Castle Black. In

00:03:48.409 --> 00:03:52.099
Book 3 they use wights to kill hundreds of
Night’s Watchmen at the Fist of the First

00:03:52.099 --> 00:03:58.049
Men , then Sam kills a walker, and later wights
are sent after Sam and Gilly. In Book 5 wights

00:03:58.049 --> 00:04:02.439
attack Bran and company , and attack Hardhome. We also learn the Others have been attacking

00:04:02.439 --> 00:04:07.250
wildlings for years , forcing them to flee
south and “hide behind [the] Wall”. So

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:11.599
the Others are killing humans of many different
groups on a large scale, and are building

00:04:11.599 --> 00:04:16.150
an army of the dead .
But that’s not all they’re doing. The

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:20.760
wildling Craster refers to the Others as “gods”,
and has a sort of an agreement with them.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:25.910
They don’t attack him and his wives , and
in return, Craster gives them his male children,

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:31.100
leaving the newborns in the snow to be collected
by the Others. In the show, there’s a scene

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:34.820
where an Other takes one of Craster’s sons
to a kind of an altar in what looks like the

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:41.350
far-north Land of Always Winter. There, the
baby is changed into what looks like an Other.

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:44.970
One of Craster’s wives refers to the Others
as “Craster’s sons”. So it looks like

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:49.880
the Others can transform humans into Others,
and that some people give their children to

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:54.530
the Others as a religious offering. It’s
probably not just Craster doing this. There

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:58.580
are all sorts of “strange” wildling cultures
further to the north, and some of them are

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:04.100
rumoured to worship “gods of snow and ice”. Sacrifice to the Others may be a widespread

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:08.950
thing. The word Others is used as a curse,
like a swear word, and the phrase is almost

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:13.150
always “The Others take you”. It’s
not ‘the Others kill you”, or ‘the Others

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:16.860
steal your stuff’ – it is sometimes ‘the
Others bugger you’ – but it’s almost

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:22.660
always “the Others take you”, suggesting
that the Others have a history of taking humans.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:27.210
We also hear stories of “wildlings who would
lay with the Others to birth half-human children”,

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:30.390
which sounds like a different thing, but
either way, the Others clearly don’t just

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:35.960
want to kill humans, but also want to use
them make more Others. Maybe that’s the

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:40.010
only way Others can reproduce, maybe this
is part of some kind of natural cycle. For

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:44.350
now, we don’t know. What we do know is that
the Others are killing people, they’re building

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:49.450
an army of the dead, and winter is coming. Melisandre says they’re “marshalling”

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:53.300
their “evil” “power” and will wage
“a war for life itself”, that they’ll

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:57.670
bring a “night that never ends”, unless
“true men” can fight them in a “great

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:01.900
battle” called “the war for the dawn”. Stannis calls the Others “The only enemy

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:06.600
that matters”. Jon calls them the “real
foe” and says “they will come for us”.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:10.950
Everyone’s expecting war between humanity
and the Others.

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:14.990
Which could make sense, because a “war for
the dawn” has apparently happened before.

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:20.280
We’re told legends of “the Long Night”
– a dark winter, thousands of years ago,

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:25.470
that lasted a generation. It’s said that
“In that darkness, the Others came”, to

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:30.410
“extinguish all light and warmth”. “They
swept over holdfasts and cities and kingdoms,

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:35.380
felled heroes and armies by the score, riding”
“monstrous ice spiders and the horses of

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:40.150
the dead”, “leading hosts of the slain”. When “the realms of men” were almost

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:43.220
at “an end”, Westeros was saved by the
“last hero”, who, with the “help”

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:47.500
of the children of the forest – who might
have given him obsidian – established the

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:51.870
Night’s Watch, and defeated the Others in
battle. After this victory, the Wall was

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:56.770
built to make sure the Others could never
came back. So that’s the story in Westeros.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:00.940
Across the Narrow Sea, the Rhoynar have legends
of a darkness, but there’s no mention of

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:05.800
the Others or a battle. In central Essos,
the Dothraki and the cultures of Slaver’s

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:10.710
Bay seem to have no tales of the Long Night.
But in the far east, there are legends very

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:14.560
similar to the one of the “last hero”
and the “battle for the dawn”. The YiTish

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:19.220
say that during the Long Night they were attacked
by the “Lion of Night” and his “demons”,

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:24.260
who were defeated when a hero called Azor
Ahai forged a burning sword and led humanity

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:30.540
into battle. Now, huge mysterious citadels
called the Five Forts stand to keep the demons

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:35.600
out, dividing the “realms of men” from
the Grey Waste beyond . Which sounds a lot

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:38.930
like the Wall, right? And the “demons”
of the “Lion of Night” sound a lot like

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:43.930
the Others. Isn’t it super weird that such
similar things happened on apparently opposite

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:48.410
sides of the world? George Martin has said
that his world is round, so if you went far

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:54.590
enough east you must eventually find Westeros. Maybe these two places, the Grey Waste and

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:59.620
the Land of Always Winter, are connected.
Maybe the Others of Westeros and the “demons”

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:04.530
of Yi Ti are one and the same, based in some
place between the Wall and the Five Forts.

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:10.200
That would make this area a centre of cold
in this world, leaving Valyria – where the

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:14.760
Targaryens and apparently dragons come from
– a centre of heat. This gives a sense of

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:18.710
order to the fire and ice in this world, and
might explain why the Long Night affected

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:24.180
Westeros and Yi Ti so badly without affecting
central Essos apparently at all. This could

00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:28.210
also be related to the irregular seasons,
which George Martin has suggested will eventually

00:08:28.210 --> 00:08:33.460
be resolved somehow. Anyway, the main legends
agree that the Long Night ended with a battle

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:37.930
led by a hero now prophesied be reborn and
save the world once more.

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:45.020
Which, y’know, could happen. Jon Snow could
be reborn with a flaming sword as Azor Ahai,

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:49.370
he could unite the Night’s Watch, the wildlings,
and the north, and lead them to war, killing

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:53.320
Others with obsidian from the children of
the forest – or from Stannis’ mines – and

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:57.000
Daenerys could fly in with her dragons, to
burn away the dead, and Tyrion could ride

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:00.620
one of the dragons, and Bran could warg one
of the other ones, and Rickon could ride in

00:09:00.620 --> 00:09:04.450
on a unicorn, and all the good guys could
come together and kill all the bad guys, and

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:08.470
Daenerys and Jon could make out, and rule
together as Queen and King, as fire and ice,

00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:15.130
for ever and ever, the end.
Except things probably won’t be that simple.

00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:19.800
Does it really make sense for this story to
end with a war? We’ve seen so much war already,

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:24.320
and most it achieves nothing but suffering.
Look at Robb Stark’s campaign, Daenerys’

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:28.670
conquests in Slaver’s Bay, Stannis’ invasion
of Blackwater Bay – they’re all seemingly

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:33.320
just wars waged by seemingly good people,
but they all fail their original goals and

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:38.050
cause a huge amount of suffering, not just
for the nobility, but for the common people.

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:42.660
Look at Arya’s chapters at Harrenhal, Jaime’s
chapters in the riverlands, at Septon Meribald’s

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:48.460
speech – we’re shown over and over that
war is terrible and wrong and pointless . George

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:52.280
Martin himself was a conscientious objector
to the Vietnam War, and many of his other

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:57.660
books also have a strong anti-war theme . So
how can a story filled with terrible, unjust,

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:01.580
pointless wars end with a great war that saves
the world?

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:05.910
A “war for the dawn” would also be too
obvious. George Martin has said that “part

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:10.010
of the thing [he] always strive[s] for in
[his] books, is not to be predictable”. And

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:13.620
what could be more predictable than the good
guys defeating the evil ice monsters in a

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:18.750
big epic battle? Martin has specifically criticised
the Lord-of-the-Rings-style war between good

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:22.130
and evil. He says “We don’t need any more
Dark Lords, we don’t need any more” “good

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:27.080
guys battling bad guys”, “the wars in
my books are much more morally complex”.

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:30.970
Showrunner David Benioff has said “it’s
not going to be your classic good-versus-evil

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:35.200
conflict”. So the writer of the series
and the creators of the show, as well as the

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:40.350
series itself make it clear that this story
won’t end with a righteous war between good

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:44.760
guys and bad guys.
Which makes you wonder – maybe that’s

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:48.750
not what happened last time either. Legends
of the Long Night and the “battle for the

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:53.160
dawn” are ancient , and weren’t even written
down until thousands of years after they supposedly

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:57.840
happened. We’re warned over and over not
to trust these tales. So while the Long Night

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:01.620
did seem to have happened, and the Others
clearly are real, the “war for the dawn”

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:05.710
might not have happened the way we’re told.
After all, it’s pretty hard to believe that

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:10.020
humanity could’ve defeated the Others – we’ve
seen how dangerous they are. Would a hero

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:14.800
with a flaming sword have been enough to win
the war? A popular idea in the fan community

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:19.220
is that the Long Night ended with some kind
of peaceful agreement between humanity and

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:24.440
the Others. Hints of this can be found at
the Nightfort.

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:28.630
The Nightfort is the oldest and the largest
of the castles on the Wall, the “chief seat

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:33.090
of the [Night’s] Watch” for “thousands
of years”. Now, it’s abandoned, and notorious

00:11:33.090 --> 00:11:37.010
as a “haunted” and “dreadful place”. It’s the subject of horror stories and

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:40.820
strange legends, some of which hint at a
connection between the Night’s Watch and

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:45.280
the Others. This brings us to the story of
the Night’s King. To clear something up

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:49.300
real quick, this white walker in the show
is referred to as the “Night King” by

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:53.150
HBO, but it’s probably not the same figure
as the legendary Night’s King, at least

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:57.460
not in the books, so keep that in mind. The
story of the Night’s King goes that thousands

00:11:57.460 --> 00:12:01.560
of years ago, the thirteenth Lord Commander
of the Night’s Watch loved a woman “with

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:06.600
skin as white as the moon and eyes like blue
stars” – which sounds like an Other or

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:11.160
a wight. He “gave his seed to her [and]
his soul as well”, he “proclaimed her

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:15.570
a queen and himself her king”, he “bound
his Sworn Brothers to his will” “with

00:12:15.570 --> 00:12:19.290
strange sorceries”, and “ruled” “For
thirteen years” until the Starks and the

00:12:19.290 --> 00:12:23.510
wildlings “joined” together to cast him
down. It was then found that the Night’s

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:27.790
King had been making “sacrifice[s] to the
Others”, which might mean giving them babies,

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:31.680
like Craster. The Night’s King was doing
this at the Nightfort, and the Nightfort just

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:36.820
happens to have a super creepy underground
“hidden” magic door called the Black Gate

00:12:36.820 --> 00:12:40.680
that lets Night’s Watchmen through the Wall. It’s likely that the Night’s King was

00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:44.850
using this sneaky door to make his secret
sacrifices. And the thing is – the Black

00:12:44.850 --> 00:12:49.610
Gate is as “old as the Wall itself”. Why
does “The greatest and oldest” of the

00:12:49.610 --> 00:12:53.050
Night’s Watch’s castles, its “chief
seat” for “thousands of years”, have

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:59.190
an in-built sneaky hidden door to beyond the
Wall? Maybe it had always been used for secret

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:03.420
sacrifice to the Others. There are several
other legends connecting this castle to the

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:08.279
Others – one about a “hero” with suspiciously
blue eyes , another about a “thing that

00:13:08.279 --> 00:13:13.100
came in the night”. It definitely seems
like some kind of shady shit involving the

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:17.600
Others was going on at the Nightfort in the
early years of the Watch. The HBO Viewer’s

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:22.180
Guide hints at a “secret” at the Nightfort
– and this secret may soon be uncovered,

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:26.690
because in Dance the Night’s Watch starts
to restore the castle for habitation. Maybe

00:13:26.690 --> 00:13:31.100
they’ll find that the Watch has a history
of sacrifice to the Others.

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:35.340
You’ve gotta wonder about the Wall itself
– we’re told that it was built to keep

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:39.080
the Others out after their defeat in the “battle
for the dawn”. But why would you build a

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:43.670
wall made of ice to stop creatures of ice?
And how could it have been built? We’re

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:48.170
told that the First Men cut the ice from frozen
lakes into huge blocks, dragged them along

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:53.190
on sledges and stacked them up into the Wall. Can you imagine how long that would take?

00:13:53.190 --> 00:13:57.279
The Great Pyramid of Giza took decades to
build that way, and the Wall is as long as

00:13:57.279 --> 00:14:02.420
two thousand Great Pyramids , much taller
too. Even with the help of giants , the Wall

00:14:02.420 --> 00:14:07.140
would have taken centuries or millennia to
build. Doesn’t it make more sense for the

00:14:07.140 --> 00:14:11.210
Others to have built the Wall – you know,
the ice creatures who we know can make things

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:15.540
out of ice? The humans, meanwhile, could have
built the nineteen castles along the Wall

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:20.190
– the structures that actually look like
they could have been built by humans. Maybe

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:24.920
the Long Night ended not with war but with
co-operation. We know from Craster that peaceful

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:29.890
agreement between humans and Others is possible,
and we have another precedent in the Pact,

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:33.630
which was a peaceful agreement between the
First Men and the children of the forest after

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:38.140
their long horrible war. Under the pact, the
children were given the forests, and the first

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:42.870
men given everything else. Maybe, similarly,
the humans and Others agreed to give the land

00:14:42.870 --> 00:14:47.339
north of the Wall to the Others, and the land
south of the Wall to the humans. A bit of

00:14:47.339 --> 00:14:52.130
sneaky human sacrifice through the Black Gate
might have been part of the deal. Of course,

00:14:52.130 --> 00:14:56.420
if there ever was an agreement between the
Others and humans, it seems long forgotten

00:14:56.420 --> 00:15:01.330
now, everyone’s gearing up for war, but
– we actually have the perfect hero to make

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:07.130
peace possible again.
Jon Snow is the Lord Commander of the Night’s

00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:11.190
Watch. He’s been on or beyond the Wall for
almost all of the series and it’s hinted

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:15.930
pretty explicitly that has some special destiny. He probably has the blood of the Targaryen

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:21.060
dragon kings as well as the Stark Kings of
Winter, he may be the prophesied Azor Ahai,

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:25.440
and he’s got some definite similarities
with Jesus. However you look at it, Jon seems

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:30.020
to be the guy who will deal with the Others.
And the thing is – Jon has a lot of experience

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:35.310
in making peace between peoples. He spends
almost all of Dance trying to reconcile the

00:15:35.310 --> 00:15:38.899
Night’s Watch and the wildlings – two
groups who hate each other, have been fighting

00:15:38.899 --> 00:15:43.610
for thousands of years , and seem totally
foreign to each other. Jon works to achieve

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:48.740
peace because he realises it’s best for
everyone. He tries to understand and sympathise

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:52.899
with the wildlings – and, similarly, he
tries to understand the Others. He keeps

00:15:52.899 --> 00:15:56.560
some wights for observation, and gets Sam
to research the Others in the Castle Black

00:15:56.560 --> 00:16:01.339
library . One of Stannis’ knights mockingly
asks if Jon would offer the Others hospitality

00:16:01.339 --> 00:16:05.130
at the Wall. Maybe that’ll actually end
up happening.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:09.210
Jon is, of course, currently bleeding in the
snow with four stab wounds, but he’ll probably

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:13.880
be resurrected by Melisandre. In the other
resurrections we’ve seen, people change

00:16:13.880 --> 00:16:19.520
when they come back from the dead, they seem
to become less human , so maybe Jon will too.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:23.220
He’ll certainly feel alienated from the
Night’s Watch who betrayed him, and he might

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:28.339
feel somehow closer to the Others. His last
line in Dance says “He never felt the fourth

00:16:28.339 --> 00:16:34.740
knife. Only the cold”. Jon Snow is someone
special in this story. He’s a hero, and

00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:39.880
a bastard in black . He’s honourable, and
he breaks his vows. He’s the son of a Stark

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:45.580
and, probably, a Targaryen. There’s a duality
in him, a meeting of ice and fire, which makes

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:50.089
him perfect to make peace between humanity
and the Others. It won’t be easy – there’ll

00:16:50.089 --> 00:16:55.410
be tough choices, compromises, sacrifices,
maybe an uncomfortable marriage , but Jon

00:16:55.410 --> 00:17:00.320
Snow seems the perfect person to do it. So
maybe, when Jon is reborn, he won’t be a

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:05.910
warrior with a burning sword, but a different
kind of hero, a greater kind of hero. Someone

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:10.920
who’ll work not to rule or destroy, but
to co-operate, and understand. Maybe Jon will

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:18.400
bring peace, and balance, to the world of
ice and fire.

00:17:18.400 --> 00:17:23.339
We first saw the Others in A Game of Thrones,
nineteen years ago. And we still don’t really

00:17:23.339 --> 00:17:28.380
know what they are and what they’re about.
But we can work some stuff out. The Others

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:33.600
are living creatures of ice that resurrect
the dead. They’re dangerous, they’re killing

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:38.390
people, and building an army of wights, but
they’re also using humans to reproduce – so

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:43.000
they’re probably not trying to wipe humans
out. Some expect a battle between humanity

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:47.800
and the Others, which has apparently happened
before, but it’d make no sense thematically

00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:53.410
for the story to end with war. An alternative
is peace, and there are hints at the Nightfort

00:17:53.410 --> 00:17:59.550
and the Wall that humans and Others somehow
got along in the past. Jon Snow might be the

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:05.660
perfect person to bring a new peace. That’s
one possibility, anyway – for more theories

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:09.350
and discussion you might like to check out
the A Song of Ice and Fire subreddit and the

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:13.790
westeros.org forums.
